            "review_title": "Review at Yakiniku Kokoro",
            "review_text": "Wolverine154\nAlbuquerque, New Mexico415 contributions\n0\nGreat & cheap Jap cuisine\nDec 2025 • Solo\nUnfortunately I lived in one of the worst countries on earth about 30 or so years ago when I was young, recently out of college, needed to make money in order to return to the US for grad school. That nation? Japan. Again, horrible country populated by mostly homogeneous & miserable citizens. BUT the saving grace was the amazing food. I learned about okonomiyaki, basically a dinner pancake w/pork, veggies, etc. which is a basic hearty commoner dish. So...I was in Ha Noi & this place was close to my hotel. I got my fix-it was single serving size. I also had the seaweed salad AND a single chocolate mochi for dessert. All was top notch AND about $5 US total. Unreal. Loved it.\nRead more\nWritten March 13, 2026",
