            "review_title": "Review at Yakiniku Kokoro",
            "review_text": "Greenlotus\nHouston, Texas75 contributions\n0\nA bit overprice, but it was worth it\nApr 2013 • Couples\nThe atmosphere is so so, as so many restaurant you can encounter in the particular Japanese + Korean street, but the food quality and service are what makes this restaurant stand out!\n\nWe came here 4 times all for lunch, and every time we ordered st grilled. The food quality is top notch, you can taste the sweetness and the tenderness of the meat and the taste does linger. However, the price is a bit much, even for the side dishes, you won't get it for free which a lot of restaurants now carry.\n\nI recommend eating here only for special occasion, since the price is really \"special\". Also, the service is attentive, only that when we ate there today, the servers (someone who I thought was the manager) kept on talking and swearing words real loud, we had to made a complain for 2 times. I would gave them 3 stars if this happens again but since this is the first time, I hope it will not reoccur.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten April 27, 2013",
